Third-party software (installed with pip, not copied into this repository)

All allow commercial use. Their license notices are included in the installed packages.

  Flask, Werkzeug, Jinja2, MarkupSafe, itsdangerous, click   BSD-3-Clause
  blinker                                                    MIT
  NumPy                                                      BSD-3-Clause (bundled parts: 0BSD, MIT, Zlib, CC0-1.0)
  PyTorch (CPU build)                                        BSD-3-Clause
    filelock, setuptools (MIT); sympy, mpmath, networkx, fsspec (BSD); typing-extensions (PSF-2.0)
  Gymnasium, Farama-Notifications                            MIT
  cloudpickle                                                BSD-3-Clause
  Stable-Baselines3, sb3-contrib                             MIT
  gunicorn (Docker only)                                     MIT
  pytest (tests only)                                        MIT

Install the CPU build of PyTorch (https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu), as the Dockerfile does.
The default Linux build of PyTorch also installs NVIDIA CUDA libraries under NVIDIA's proprietary
license; this app does not need them.

Docker base image: python:3.12-slim (Python: PSF-2.0; Debian packages under their own free licenses,
with sources available from Debian).

Fonts: Instrument Sans (Copyright 2022 The Instrument Sans Project Authors) and JetBrains Mono
(Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors), SIL Open Font License 1.1, commercial use allowed.
Served by the app from studio/static/fonts (Latin subset from Fontsource); the license texts are
studio/static/fonts/OFL-*.txt. No font or other file is loaded from an external server.

